// Lets unattended-upgrades install from the local repository in /usr/local/lib/debs. It pins every repository it is
// not allowed to use to -32768, and switches a candidate from such a repository to the newest version in an allowed
// one. For a patched package that would be Ubuntu's unpatched security update, installed as soon as Ubuntu publishes
// it. Allowed, the local repository keeps the 1001 it is pinned at, so a patched package stays on its patched build
// until the rebuild succeeds.
//
// rebuild-patched-packages holds every package of the local repository but the rebuilds of versions unattended-upgrades
// would install by itself, in 53unattended-upgrades-local-holds, so that the next apt upgrade installs the others. See
// Unattended upgrades in rebuild-patched-packages.
//
// The repository is matched by its empty site, which only a local repository has.
